### Drill 5: Cloud-Native Ceph Dynamic Shared Storage Alternatives

When using Ceph as the cluster storage backend (`storage_nfs_provider: "ceph"`), candidates and administrators have two cloud-native alternatives for dynamic ReadWriteMany shared storage:

#### Approach A: Ceph NFS via NFS CSI (`03-ceph-nfs-sc.yaml`)

Consumes the Ceph NFS-Ganesha daemon export (`nfs-server.local:/exports`) using the standard NFS CSI driver:

#### Step 1: Apply Ceph NFS StorageClass

```bash
cd {{ cka_lab_storage_classes_dir }}/02-storage-classes

kubectl apply -f 03-ceph-nfs-sc.yaml
kubectl get storageclass {{ cka_lab_ceph_nfs_storage_class | default('ceph-nfs-csi') }}
```

#### Step 2: Deploy Dynamic RWX PVC & Multi-Replica Workload

```bash
kubectl apply -f 04-ceph-dynamic-pvc.yaml
kubectl apply -f 05-ceph-shared-deployment.yaml
kubectl rollout status deployment/ceph-nfs-shared-app --timeout=60s
```

#### Approach B: Native CephFS Shared Filesystem (`03-cephfs-sc.yaml`)

Directly uses Ceph's native distributed filesystem driver (`rook-ceph.cephfs.csi.ceph.com`), bypassing NFS translation layers:

#### Step 3: Apply Native CephFS StorageClass

```bash
kubectl apply -f 03-cephfs-sc.yaml
kubectl get storageclass {{ cka_lab_cephfs_storage_class | default('rook-cephfs') }}
```

